      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a decent start, but it's a bit too \"wall of text\" for what I'm looking for. Even though I warned you about the junk feedback from the automated checker, the CI/CD actually flagged this draft because the \"comprehensiveness score\" was incredibly low—it basically failed the initial pass.\n\nCan you expand this out? I need it to look more robust for the pipeline, but like I said, don't make it unreadable. Just try to add more logical structure, maybe some specific steps for installation or authentication, and use more headings or lists to make the key points stand out better so the scanner picks it up. Keep it professional though.",
      "source": "evaluator"
